1. Work performed

Cached host tensor scales were added to [nvfp4_weight.h](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/include/nemotron/nvfp4_weight.h), [nvfp4_weight.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/nvfp4_weight.cpp), [device_nvfp4_matrix.h](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/include/nemotron/device_nvfp4_matrix.h), [device_nvfp4_matrix.cu](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/device_nvfp4_matrix.cu), and [monolithic_expert_weights.cu](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/monolithic_expert_weights.cu). Weight tensor scales are now captured from host data at upload time, monolithic expert weights keep a host-side per-expert scale vector, and packed activations cache one D2H tensor-scale read per pack instead of per GEMM.

The NVFP4 hot path in [expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp) now passes cached host tensor scales into [nvfp4_gemm_runner.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/nvfp4_gemm_runner.cpp), so the decode path no longer does the two per-GEMM `cudaMemcpy(..., cudaMemcpyDeviceToHost)` reads for alpha. `RunNvfp4RowMajorFp32AccumToDevice(...)` now computes `alpha` from host floats, dropped the per-GEMM `output->FillZero()` because `beta=0`, and caches the cuBLASLt matmul descriptor/layout/heuristic in a thread-local runner cache keyed by handle/device/shape/layout/workspace.

2. Compile status

All requested builds passed when run sequentially:

- `cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target nemotron_runtime_backend -j4`
- `cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target full_forward_manifest_smoke_test -j4`
- `cmake --build build-benchmarks --target nano_fused_decode_bench -j4`

3. Any concerns

The first attempt to build the two `build-phase1-tests` targets in parallel hit an archive race because both commands were writing the same build tree at once; rerunning sequentially passed cleanly. Also, I kept backward-compatible runner overloads for non-hot-path callers, so only the updated decode path is guaranteed to avoid the old D2H fallback.
